# ControlRig Stable Authoring Phase 4 Live Proof

Date: 2026-06-30

Scope: one commandlet smoke for the Phase 4 Piper stable fixture. This proof is
limited to the sample/temp target declared by the fixture recipe:
`/Game/_MCP_Temp/ControlRigStable/CR_Piper_StablePrototype`.

## Ieta Boundary

- Original assets remain read-only.
- The only allowed live target is under `/Game/_MCP_Temp`.
- The fixture keeps `save=false`; no stable fixture `.uasset` is promoted.
- No solver unit expansion is part of this proof.
- No AnimBP binding or input-default promotion is part of this proof.

## Command

```powershell
$Project = (Resolve-Path .\MCPGameProject\MCPGameProject.uproject).ProviderPath
$Script = (Resolve-Path .\MCPGameProject\Plugins\UnrealMCP\Scripts\ControlRig\smoke_controlrig_stable_fixture.py).ProviderPath
& 'C:\Program Files\Epic Games\UE_5.6\Engine\Binaries\Win64\UnrealEditor-Cmd.exe' $Project -run=pythonscript -script="$Script" -unattended -nop4 -nosplash -nosound -NullRHI -log
```

## Result

The commandlet exited with status `0`.

Important log lines:

- `LogPythonScriptCommandlet: Display: Python script executed successfully`
- `LogInit: Display: Success - 0 error(s), 5 warning(s)`
- `LogTemp: Display: UnrealMCPBridge: Server stopped`

The warnings were non-fatal commandlet/startup warnings. The missing
`/Game/_MCP_Temp/ControlRigStable/CR_Piper_StablePrototype` package warning
matched the expected first-run state where there was no pre-existing temp asset
to delete.

## Post-Run Boundary Checks

- `git status --short -- MCPGameProject\Content MCPGameProject\Plugins\UnrealMCP\Content` reported no tracked content changes.
- No saved `MCPGameProject/Content/_MCP_Temp/ControlRigStable` asset file was present after the run.
- No Unreal Editor process remained running.
- No listener remained on the UE 5.6.1 UnrealMCP bridge port `55561`.

## Interpretation

The Phase 4 stable fixture smoke passed as a live sample/temp proof without
persisting a generated fixture asset. This does not approve original asset
mutation, solver unit expansion, AnimBP binding, or stable input-default
promotion. This live proof does not approve solver work. The Phase 5 solver expansion boundary is tracked separately in
`Docs/Analysis/controlrig_stable_authoring_phase5_contract.md`.
